  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Farmer-Led Irrigation Development Learning Study in FDW Projects</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment reviews farmer-led irrigation development (FLID) approaches in selected Sustainable Water Fund (FDW) projects to better understand factors influencing the sustainability and scaling of smallholder irrigation initiatives. Through project workshops, diagnostics and comparative analysis, the study identifies lessons learned, best practices and challenges related to irrigation technologies, markets, finance and policy conditions. The findings will support consolidation strategies for ongoing projects and inform future programmes aimed at improving water efficiency and livelihoods for smallholder farmers.</narrative>
  </description>
